    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44118" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">siccānĕus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		siccus (a technical word of Columella); of soil, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>dry</i>, <i>of a dry nature</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus prati (opp. riguum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 16, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locus (opp. riguus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					4, 30, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">11, 2,
				71</span></i>.—<i>Neutr. plur. absol.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de siccaneis et riguis non comperimus,</span>”
				<i>dry places</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 2, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
